  ('43', 'imitation furskins obtained by weaving (woven pile fabrics simulating fur)', '58', '5801', 'Note 5', 'Throughout this Schedule, the expression "artificial fur" means any imitation of furskin consisting of wool, hair or other fibres gummed or sewn on to leather, woven fabric or other materials, but does not include imitation furskins obtained by weaving or knitting (generally, heading 5801 or 6001).'),
