  ('48', 'paper, paperboard, cellulose wadding and articles thereof, printed with motifs, characters or pictorial representations, which are not merely subsidiary to the primary use of the goods (except for the goods of heading 4814 or 4821)', '49', NULL, 'Note 12', 'Except for the goods of heading 4814 or 4821 , paper, paperboard, cellulose wadding and articles thereof, printed with motifs, characters or pictorial representations, which are not merely subsidiary to the primary use of the goods, fall in Chapter 49.'),
  ('48', 'filter paper or paperboard (including tea-bag paper) or felt paper or paperboard (heading 4802 does not cover these)', NULL, NULL, 'Note 5', 'Heading 4802 does not, however, cover filter paper or paperboard (including tea-bag paper) or felt paper or paperboard.'),
  ('48', 'loose sheets or cards, cut to size, whether or not printed, embossed or perforated (heading 4820 does not cover these)', NULL, NULL, 'Note 10', 'Heading 4820 does not cover loose sheets or cards, cut to size, whether or not printed, embossed or perforated.'),
  ('49', 'photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases', '37', NULL, 'Note 1', 'This Chapter does not cover : (a) photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases (Chapter 37) ; (b) maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed (heading 9023) ; (c) playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95 ; or (d) original engravings, prints or lithographs (heading 9702), postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like of heading 9704, antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97'),
  ('49', 'maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed', '90', '9023', 'Note 1', 'This Chapter does not cover : (a) photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases (Chapter 37) ; (b) maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed (heading 9023) ; (c) playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95 ; or (d) original engravings, prints or lithographs (heading 9702), postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like of heading 9704, antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97'),
  ('49', 'playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95', '95', NULL, 'Note 1', 'This Chapter does not cover : (a) photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases (Chapter 37) ; (b) maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed (heading 9023) ; (c) playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95 ; or (d) original engravings, prints or lithographs (heading 9702), postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like of heading 9704, antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97'),
  ('49', 'original engravings, prints or lithographs', '97', '9702', 'Note 1', 'This Chapter does not cover : (a) photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases (Chapter 37) ; (b) maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed (heading 9023) ; (c) playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95 ; or (d) original engravings, prints or lithographs (heading 9702), postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like of heading 9704, antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97'),
  ('49', 'postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like', '97', '9704', 'Note 1', 'This Chapter does not cover : (a) photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases (Chapter 37) ; (b) maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed (heading 9023) ; (c) playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95 ; or (d) original engravings, prints or lithographs (heading 9702), postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like of heading 9704, antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97'),
  ('49', 'antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97', '97', NULL, 'Note 1', 'This Chapter does not cover : (a) photographic negatives or positives on transparent bases (Chapter 37) ; (b) maps, plans or globes, in relief, whether or not printed (heading 9023) ; (c) playing cards or other goods of Chapter 95 ; or (d) original engravings, prints or lithographs (heading 9702), postage or revenue stamps, stamppostmarks, first-day covers, postal stationery or the like of heading 9704, antiques of an age exceeding one hundred years or other articles of Chapter 97'),
  ('49', 'printed pictures or illustrations not bearing a text, whether in the form of signatures or separate sheets', '49', '4911', 'Note 4', 'Heading 4901 also covers : (a) a collection of printed reproductions of, for example, works of art or drawings, with a relative text, put up with numbered pages in a form suitable for binding into one or more volumes ; (b) a pictorial supplement accompanying, and subsidiary to, a bound volume ; and (c) printed parts of books or booklets, in the form of assembled or separate sheets or signatures, constituting the whole or a part of a complete work and designed for binding. However, printed pictures or illustrations not bearing a text, whether in the form of signatures or separate sheets, fall in heading 4911.'),
  ('49', 'publications which are essentially devoted to advertising (for example, brochures, pamphlets, leaflets, trade catalogues, year books published by trade associations, tourist propaganda)', '49', '4911', 'Note 5', 'Subject to Note 3 to this Chapter, heading 4901 does not cover publications which are essentially devoted to advertising (for example, brochures, pamphlets, leaflets, trade catalogues, year books published by trade associations, tourist propaganda). Such publications are to be classified in heading 4911.'),
