  ('69', 'articles NOT fired after shaping — including ceramic articles heated to less than 800°C for resin curing, hydration acceleration, or volatile removal — are excluded from Chapter 69 by Note 1(b). Such unfired or low-temperature-cured articles typically fall to Chapter 38 (miscellaneous chemical products) or back to the raw clay/material chapter (e.g., Ch.25 for unfired kaolin/clays).', NULL, NULL, 'Note 1(b)', '(b) articles heated to temperatures less than 800C for purposes such as curing of resins, accelerating hydration reactions, or for the removal of water or other volatile components, are not considered to be fired. Such articles are excluded from Chapter 69'),
