  ('74', 'Copper phosphide (phosphor copper) containing more than 15% by weight of phosphorous — excluded from Chapter 74 master alloys (Chapter Note 1(c)) and classified as a separate chemical compound', '28', '2853', 'Chapter Note 1(c)', '(c) Master alloys: Alloys containing with other elements more than 10 per cent by weight, of copper not usefully malleable and commonly used as an additive in the manufacture of other alloys or as deoxidants, de-sulphuring agents or for similar uses in the metallurgy of non-ferrous metals. However, copper phosphide (phosphor copper) containing more than 15% by weight of phosphorous falls in heading 2853.'),
  ('74', 'Wirebars and billets of Chapter 74 with their ends tapered or otherwise worked simply to facilitate their entry into machines for converting them into drawing stock (wire-rod) or tubes — these are treated as UNWROUGHT COPPER and remain in heading 7403, not as bars/rods of heading 7407', '74', '7403', 'Section Note 9(a)', 'Wirebars and billets of Chapter 74 with their ends tapered or otherwise worked simply to facilitate their entry into machines for converting them into, for example, drawing stock (wire-rod) or tubes, are however to be taken to be unwrought copper of heading 7403.'),
